{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>If there be laid on him a ransom.</b> This <b>if</b> is not uncertainty but obligation, like (Exodus 22:24) אם כסף תלוה. And every ransom is an atonement, in the manner of the offerings. And they do not force him to come to the court to obligate him in this, and even if they did obligate him they do not seize his property." "<b>And he shall give the redemption of his life, according to all that is laid upon him.</b> This teaches that if he gave, according to all that is laid upon him, the redemption of his life, then he is saved, as it says (Job 33:24) ״פדעהו מרדת שחת מצאתי כופר״. And this law applies to those liable to death by the hand of Heaven, such as this one who did not kill but was the cause of his ox killing by not guarding it — he has redemption. But one who kills has no redemption, as it says (Leviticus 27:29) ״אך כל חרם אשר יחרם מן האדם לא יפדה מות יומת״."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:02:45.256899414Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}